+// Fix 156i (Fighters Uncaged 5553084E #67, Zumba Fitness Core #63): a skeleton frame carries
+// the number of the depth frame it was tracked from, as the console's NUI does. Fighters
+// Uncaged's per-frame fetch (821A1148) keeps the largest frame number of its skeleton, depth
+// and color frames and takes a new one from a source only when that source's number differs;
+// the virtual skeleton was numbered on its own clock (33 ms periods since the skeleton source
+// started), the depth frames on the camera's (since the camera opened), so the numbers never
+// met and the title saw no body ("No body detected"), except while the Guide paused its image
+// streams. The number of the last depth frame the camera delivered; before the first one, the
+// skeleton's own period.
+inline uint32_t SkeletonFrameNumber(uint32_t last_depth_frame, uint32_t period) {
+  return last_depth_frame ? last_depth_frame : period;
+}
